# outline_user

Retrieves an existing Outline workspace account. Configure exactly one of `id` or `email`. Both attributes are optional and computed, so the lookup returns the attribute you did not configure as well.

ID lookup accepts a canonical lowercase, nonzero user UUID. Email lookup compares the exact lowercase, normalized email across every page of the admin-visible user list, including pending and suspended accounts. It does not accept substring or display-name matches. No match or more than one match produces an error; use a UUID when emails are ambiguous. Equivalent configured email casing is preserved in state.

Use an unrestricted API key owned by an active admin. The data source targets Outline 1.10.1 only. It does not invite, activate, suspend, or modify accounts, manage memberships, or configure authentication. Use the [user resource](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/glitchedmob/outline/latest/docs/resources/user) to manage an account and the [OIDC guide](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/glitchedmob/outline/latest/docs/guides/oidc) for provisioning before SSO sign-in.

## Example usage

{{ tffile "examples/data-sources/outline_user/data-source.tf" }}

Replace the example UUID with an existing account's ID. Each lookup returns `id`, `email`, `name`, `role`, and `suspended`.

A missing `users.info` target returns `403 authorization_error` in Outline 1.10.1. The provider only reports it as missing after independently verifying an active admin and checking the complete `filter = all` user list, including suspended accounts. A bare 403 does not prove absence. A listed UUID, failed check, or malformed pagination preserves the API error. An unexpected `users.info` 404 also requires the complete list check; a missing route or proxy response does not prove account deletion.

